 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`rigidity` (TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/Rigidity.lean:186-190) requires only `[IsSeparated Z.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType Z.hom]` on the target, and `class IsProper : Prop extends IsSeparated f, UniversallyClosed f, LocallyOfFiniteType f` (mathlib/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/Morphisms/Proper.lean:42) supplies both for an abelian variety. The proof body (lines 58-72) touches `B` only through `\u03b7[B.toOver]`, `\u03bc`, `GrpObj.comp_div`, `div_self'`, `div_eq_one` \u2014 all available from `GrpObj B`; `IsCommMonObj` is never used.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/AbelianVariety/Hom/Rigidity.lean",
   "fix": "State it for an unbundled target: `theorem isMonHom_of_one_hom {A : AbelianVariety K} {B : Over (Spec (.of K))} [GrpObj B] [IsSeparated B.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType B.hom] (f : A.toOver \u27f6 B) (hf : \u03b7[A.toOver] \u226b f = \u03b7[B]) : IsMonHom f`, with the same proof. The current `{A B : AbelianVariety K}` form is then a specialization needing no extra work, since `AbelianVariety.isProper` gives both instances; `equivPointed` is unchanged.",
   "issue": "`isMonHom_of_one_hom` requires `B : AbelianVariety K`, but the only facts about `B` used are `GrpObj B` (for the defect `h` and `GrpObj.comp_div`/`div_eq_one`) and, via `rigidity`'s `Z` hypotheses, `IsSeparated B.toOver.hom` and `LocallyOfFiniteType B.toOver.hom`. `B`'s properness, geometric integrality and commutativity are unused, so the statement is restricted to abelian-variety targets where any separated group scheme locally of finite type over `K` works.",
   "line": "56"
  }
 ],
